WEBVTT

00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:30.791
as space and time.

00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:32.702
This particular squashing effect

00:03:32.702 --> 00:03:35.251
is known as Lorentz contraction.

00:03:35.251 --> 00:03:36.728
Okay, but I still don't look thin.

00:03:36.728 --> 00:03:38.160
No, yes, you do.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.348
Now that we know better about space-time,

00:03:40.348 --> 00:03:41.484
we should redraw

00:03:41.484 --> 00:03:43.650
what the scene looked like to me.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.992
To you, I appear Lorentz contracted.

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:49.760
Oh but to you, I appear Lorentz contracted.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:50.845
Yes.

00:03:50.845 --> 00:03:53.344
Uh, well, at least it's fair.

00:03:53.344 --> 00:03:54.755
And speaking of fairness,

00:03:54.755 --> 00:03:56.899
just as space gets muddled with time,

00:03:56.899 --> 00:03:59.442
time also gets muddled with space,

00:03:59.442 --> 00:04:02.029
in an effect known as time dilation.